    title: "Why has Brazil accused the US of election interference?",
    summary: "The Latin American country will vote for its next president, as Lula da Silva and Bolsonaro clash over sovereignty, security and ties with Washington.",
    preview: "In Brazils upcoming presidential election, President Luiz InÃ¡cio Lula da Silva is facing right-wing challenger and ally of Donald Trump, Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former President Jair Bolsonaro. Washington has backed closer ties with Brazils right wing, while Lula da Silva has accused Bolsonaros camp of encouraging foreign interference. The election has raised questions about US influence, trade tariffs, organised crime and Brazils sovereignty. The BBC's Ione Wells explains.",
    body: "In Brazils upcoming presidential election, President Luiz InÃ¡cio Lula da Silva is facing right-wing challenger and ally of Donald Trump, Flavio Bolsonaro, son of former President Jair Bolsonaro.\n\nWashington has backed closer ties with Brazils right wing, while Lula da Silva has accused Bolsonaros camp of encouraging foreign interference.\n\nThe election has raised questions about US influence, trade tariffs, organised crime and Brazils sovereignty.\n\nThe BBC's Ione Wells explains.\n\nRelated topics\n\n- Luiz Inacio Lula da SilvaUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- BrazilUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Donald TrumpUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- Jair BolsonaroUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.\n\n- United StatesUpdates from your News topics will appear in My News and in a collection on the News homepage.",
